true particle size. 'relative to peak' (|p(Dmax)|/max|p(r)|) should be
small (e.g. <0.02-0.05) once Dmax is large enough -- if it's still a
sizeable fraction of the peak, p(r) has not decayed and Dmax is still
truncating real structure.

